  "key": "pr-885",
  "fields": {
    "summary": "test: retry the port-release proof-bind in openrouter oauth timeout test",
    "description": "Closes nothing (test-infra only).\n\n## Why\nThe `openrouter_oauth_callback_server_test.dart` timeout test asserts the port is released by re-binding it immediately after `await server.close()`. On loaded CI runners the OS release lags the awaited close — the same-process double bind then fails with `SocketException: the shared flag to bind() needs to be true`. Four CI occurrences today (PR #852 twice pre-pause, once again on the fresh head, plus cancelled churn).\n\n## What\nBounded retry (~2s, 20×100ms) around the proof-bind instead of asserting instant release. A genuinely stuck release still rethrows — the contract (close releases the port) is still asserted, just without the race. No product code touched."
